            <ArticleTitle>Coccygeoplasty: treatment for fractures of the coccyx.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>909-12</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Percutaneous vertebroplasty and sacroplasty are becoming common modalities of treatment for vertebral body compression fractures and sacral insufficiency fractures, respectively. The present report describes a case of a coccygeal fracture treated with injection of polymethylmethacrylate cement, which resulted in immediate relief of symptoms. It is suggested that this procedure be called coccygeoplasty.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
